      "page_id": "p01",
      "text": "Fruit is mostly juice. Cut a plum or a melon, and the juice runs out.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_091/pages/p01.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/pages/p01.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 6295,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/song/p01.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 8045
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p02",
      "text": "A fruit's skin is its suit. That suit holds the juice in and keeps bugs out.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_091/pages/p02.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/pages/p02.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 6817,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/song/p02.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 8411
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p03",
      "text": "Drop that fruit and it gets a bruise: cells burst inside and juice leaks.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_091/pages/p03.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/pages/p03.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 6399,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/song/p03.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 7209
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p04",
      "text": "A bruise turns brown. But a bruise is not rot! Bruised fruit is still fine to eat.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_091/pages/p04.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/pages/p04.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 8045,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/song/p04.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 9586
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p05",
      "text": "Cut the bruise off, or drop that soft fruit in a juicer for juice.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_091/pages/p05.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/pages/p05.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 5407,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/song/p05.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 6426
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p06",
      "text": "In a village, fruit is picked and sold the same day. Village fruit has no time to bruise.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_091/pages/p06.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/pages/p06.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 7732,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/song/p06.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 8411
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p07",
      "text": "Fruit that must travel takes a slow cruise in a cold ship, not a suitcase.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_091/pages/p07.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/pages/p07.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 6556,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/song/p07.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 8411
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p08",
      "text": "A fruit's sweet juice is bait. Birds eat the fruit and drop its seeds far off.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_091/pages/p08.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/pages/p08.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 6713,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/song/p08.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 7392
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p09",
      "text": "Thick juice has bits in it. Thin juice has none. Two juices come from the same fruit.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_091/pages/p09.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/pages/p09.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 7079,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_091/audio/song/p09.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 8986
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p10",
      "text": "So hunt for a bruise, and eat that fruit first. A bruise is a hint: this fruit is juicy and ripe!",
